Rule 5 (when aggregating to top-k, k cannot exceed the size of the reduction dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int, v_3 : int, v_4 : bool} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ v_3 ≥ 0 ∧ if v_4 then v_3 ≤ shape(v_1, if v_2 = -1 then ndim(v_1) - 1 else v_2)
>>
Rule 6 (reduction_input_size_override is either -1 or positive; if positive, it must be at least k)
{v_1 : int, v_2 : int} |= (v_1 = -1 ∨ v_1 > 0) ∧ v_2 ≥ 0 ∧ if v_1 > 0 then v_1 ≥ v_2
>>
Rule 7 (the effective reduction dimension must have positive size)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ shape(v_1, if v_2 = -1 then ndim(v_1) - 1 else v_2) ≥ 1
